      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the problem is clinical, not administrative. 6,400 mg of ibuprofen per day is twice the maximum labeled dose. It could seriously harm the patient, and I don't know of any standard indication for it. I also can't verify that a licensed prescriber has reviewed it, and that review is what the order needs.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **A prescriber can enter it directly.** Pharmacy and safety checks would then apply, and the prescriber would be accountable for the order.\n- **I can enter a standard dose** if the prescriber gives me one. The maximum is 800 mg by mouth 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day).\n- **I can enter a note** asking the treating clinician to review the patient's analgesic or anti-inflammatory plan.\n\nIf the treating clinician tells me what they want, I'll enter an order that fits within safe dosing limits."
      }
